      "snowpackStructure": {
        "comment": "In particular in the northwest 15 to 30 cm of snow fell in the last few days above approximately 1300 m. <br/> As a consequence of the occasionally strong northerly wind, the snow drift accumulations have increased in size during the last few days. <br/> Above approximately 2200 m there are 70 to 140 cm of snow, and even as much as 180 cm in some localities, especially above approximately 2500 m. <br/> During the sunny day, the surface snow becomes moist below 2500 m. In some places, where the wind has had a greater effect, it has a chalky consistency. <br/> It is not distinctly layered. Towards its base, the snowpack is moist, in particular below approximately 2300 m."
      },
